      "writtenOn": "2026-08-03T09:26:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i meant creating a separate API like `AddObjectDynamic` and then either pass `true` or `false` as an additional parameter. Preferably documenting this new API in PDI also.\n\nThen in the future existing callers of `AddObject` can migrate to the new API.\n\n\nTunneling D-Bus parameters over json is not the conventional implementation and in this case it\u0027s not required for the implementation.\n\n\u003e OpenBMC has quite a modular structure, consisting of small daemons with a\nlimited set of responsibilities. These communicate over D-Bus with other\ncomponents, to implement the complete BMC system.\n\nThis is from toplevel documentation https://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#structure\n\nand i interpret that to mean \u0027prefer D-Bus communication over other forms of interfacing\u0027 which would include files, tunneling via json, ...\n\n\nLet\u0027s hear what Matt Spinler has to say on the overall direction, i don\u0027t want to give you any useless feedback which might be overturned anyways.",
